 "text": "{\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"stem\": \"计算：$12.5 \\\\times 0.8 + \\\\frac{3}{4} \\\\div 0.25$\",\n      \"answer\": \"13\",\n      \"solution\": \"先算乘除：$12.5 \\\\times 0.8 = 10$，$\\\\frac{3}{4} \\\\div 0.25 = 0.75 \\\\div 0.25 = 3$。再算加法：$10 + 3 = 13$。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stem\": \"解方程：$x - \\\\frac{2}{5}x = 12.6$\",\n      \"answer\": \"21\",\n      \"solution\": \"合并同类项得 $\\\\frac{3}{5}x = 12.6$，即 $0.6x = 12.6$。两边同时除以0.6，得 $x = 21$。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stem\": \"简便计算：$99 \\\\times \\\\frac{7}{100} + 0.07$\",\n      \"answer\": \"7\",\n      \"solution\": \"将分数化为小数或提取公因数。$\\\\frac{7}{100} = 0.07$。原式变为 $99 \\\\times 0.07 + 1 \\\\times 0.07 = (99+1) \\\\times 0.07 = 100 \\\\times 0.07 = 7$。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stem\": \"计算：$(\\\\frac{5}{6} + \\\\frac{7}{12}) \\\\div \\\\frac{1}{4} - 2.5$\",\n      \"answer\": \"4.25\",\n      \"solution\": \"括号内通分：$\\\\frac{10}{12} + \\\\frac{7}{12} = \\\\frac{17}{12}$。除以 $\\\\frac{1}{4}$ 等于乘以4：$\\\\frac{17}{12} \\\\times 4 = \\\\frac{17}{3}$。最后减去2.5（即$\\\\frac{5}{2}$）：$\\\\frac{17}{3} - \\\\frac{5}{2} = \\\\frac{34-15}{6} = \\\\frac{19}{6}$。此处修正题目以确保整数或有限小数答案更佳，若按原题结果为 $3\\\\frac{1}{6}$ 或约3.17。为保证六年级常见考点，调整解析逻辑：$\\\\frac{17}{3} \\\\approx 5.67$, $5.67 - 2.5 = 3.17$。若追求整除，通常题目设计为 $(\\\\frac{5}{6} + \\\\frac{7}{12}) \\\\times 4 - 2.5 = \\\\frac{17}{3} - \\\\frac{5}{2} = \\\\frac{19}{6}$。这里保留分数形式答案或小数近似。为了符合“最终答案”简洁性，我们修改题目数字使其整除：$(\\\\frac{1}{2} + \\\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\div \\\\frac{1}{4} - 2.5$。新计算：$\\\\frac{3}{4} \\\\times 4 - 2.5 = 3 - 2.5 = 0.5$。故更新题目为：$(\\\\frac{1}{2} + \\\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\div 0.25 - 2.5$\",\n      \"answer\": \"0.5\",\n      \"solution\": \"括号内 $\\\\frac{1}{2} + \\\\frac{1}{4} = 0.75$。$0.75 \\\\div 0.25 = 3$。$3 - 2.5 = 0.5$。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stem\": \"甲数是24，乙数是甲数的 $\\\\frac{3}{4}$，丙数比乙数多2.5。求丙数。\",\n      \"answer\": \"20.5\",\n      \"solution\": \"乙数 $= 24 \\\\times \\\\frac{3}{4} = 18$。丙数 $= 18 + 2.5 = 20.5$。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stem\": \"计算：$1 \\\\div (\\\\frac{1}{2} + 0.25) \\\\times \\\\frac{8}{15}$\",\n      \"answer\": \"\\\\frac{32}{45}\",\n      \"solution\": \"括号内 $\\\\frac{1}{2} + 0.25 = 0.5 + 0.25 = 0.75 = \\\\frac{3}{4}$。$1 \\\\div \\\\frac{3}{4} = \\\\frac{4}{3}$。$\\\\frac{4}{3} \\\\times \\\\frac{8}{15} = \\\\frac{32}{45}$。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stem\": \"一根绳子长12米，第一次剪去全长的 $\\\\frac{1}{3}$，第二次剪去2.5米，还剩多少米？\",\n      \"answer\": \"5.5\",\n      \"solution\": \"第一次剪去：$12 \\\\times \\\\frac{1}{3} = 4$米。剩余：$12 - 4 = 8$米。第二次剪去2.5米后剩余：$8 - 2.5 = 5.5$米。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stem\": \"已知 $a = 0.6$，$b = \\\\frac{2}{3}$，求 $a \\\\times b \\\\div (a + b)$ 的值。（结果用最简分数表示）\",\n      \"answer\": \"\\\\frac{1}{4}\",\n      \"solution\": \"$a = \\\\frac{3}{5}$，$b = \\\\frac{2}{3}$。$a \\\\times b = \\\\frac{3}{5} \\\\times \\\\frac{2}{3} = \\\\frac{2}{5}$。$a + b = \\\\frac{9}{15} + \\\\frac{10}{15} = \\\\frac{19}{15}$。原式 $= \\\\frac{2}{5} \\\\div \\\\frac{19}{15} = \\\\frac{2}{5} \\\\times \\\\frac{15}{19} = \\\\frac{6}{19}$。等等，重新检查计算。$a+b = 0.6 + 0.66...$ 不好算。换一组数据确保整洁。设 $a=0.5, b=\\\\frac{1}{4}$。$a \\\\times b = \\\\frac{1}{2} \\\\times \\\\frac{1}{4} = \\\\frac{1}{8}$。$a+b = \\\\frac{3}{4}$。$\\\\frac{1}{8} \\\\div \\\\frac{3}{4} = \\\\frac{1}{8} \\\\times \\\\frac{4}{3} = \\\\frac{1}{6}$。故修改题目为：已知 $a=0.5, b=\\\\frac{1}{4}$，求 $a \\\\times b \\\\div (a+b)$\",\n      \"answer\": \"\\\\frac{1}{6}\",\n      \"solution\": \"$a=\\\\frac{1}{2}, b=\\\\frac{1}{4}$。分子：$\\\\frac{1}{2} \\\\times \\\\frac{1}{4} = \\\\frac{1}{8}$。分母：$\\\\frac{1}{2} + \\\\frac{1}{4} = \\\\frac{3}{4}$。结果：$\\\\frac{1}{8} \\\\div \\\\frac{3}{4} = \\\\frac{1}{8} \\\\times \\\\frac{4}{3} = \\\\frac{1}{6}$。\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
